      <p>Maine Policy Updates used an even more explicit “fact check” format. Five captured pages asked whether Republican Sen. Susan Collins lowered prescription-drug costs, funded rural hospitals, supported firefighters and first responders, secured clean-water funding and helped with home-heating costs. Each delivered a favorable conclusion. Those themes also appear on <a href="https://www.collins.senate.gov/issues" rel="noopener noreferrer">Collins’s official issue pages</a> and <a href="https://susancollins.com/get-the-facts/did-susan-collins-fund-rural-hospitals/" rel="noopener noreferrer">campaign material</a>.</p>

      <EvidenceFigure
        number={3}
        src={`${figureBase}/figure-10-maine-policy-updates-susan-collins-rural-hospitals.png`}
        alt="Maine Policy Updates fact check crediting Susan Collins with rural-hospital funding."
